SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Cruelest Game" by Matthew Futterman
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left\nSt
 atus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/201348\n\nCelebrate an unforgettable summer of tennis with an inside loo
 k at the game beyond center court. Join acclaimed sports journalist and be
 stselling author Matthew Futterman for his first Boston appearance on the 
 book tour for The Cruelest Game\, an illuminating exploration of the ambit
 ion\, resilience\, and sacrifice required to succeed at the highest levels
  of professional tennis. Through remarkable access and previously untold s
 tories\, Futterman pulls back the curtain on the sport to examine the imme
 nse pressures facing established champions and the next generation of play
 ers competing for their place among tennis’s elite.\n\nJoining Futterman
  in conversation are former world No. 7 tennis player and Olympic silver m
 edalist\, Tim Mayotte\, and The New Yorker staff writer\, Louisa Thomas\, 
 who pens the publication’s Sporting Scene column. Together\, they will b
 ring perspectives from the court and the press box to a wide-ranging conve
 rsation about professional tennis at a pivotal moment. As familiar legends
  make way for a new generation of stars\, the evening will explore the cha
 nging landscape of the sport\, the realities behind its most celebrated vi
 ctories\, and the personal price of pursuing greatness on the world stage.
  \n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complime
 ntary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all 
 cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
